    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\n1.18.3-rc1\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n_No response_\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.20\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.10.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox while running Wayland compositor\n2. Set auto away to any number\n3. Do not touch mouse or keyboard for at least that length of time\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nqTox does not auto switch my status to away when reaching the set time while using Wayland.  it works fine on x11.  My other apps properly switch to idle/away and my screensaver comes on.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nqTox should switch to away status when reaching the time configured in settings.\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nKDE Plasma - Happens on all window managers while using wayland\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```",
